 "schema": 4,
 "question": "B. Is this measure already running in South Karelia wellbeing services county (or in the HUS university hospital area that treats its patients)?\nA. Does recent evidence support the size of effect we assume: does this measure raise the share of lung cancer patients who get curative-intent treatment, and by how much?\nMeasure: Video MDT review of every stage I-III patient with the university hospital. Every patient whose cancer has not spread (stage I-III) is discussed by video with the university hospital lung team (surgeon, radiotherapy doctor, oncologist) before anyone decides against treatment that aims to cure. Today a county hospital can decide alone.",
 "area_id": "11",
 "verdict": "mixed",
 "effect_check": "weaker",
 "effect_summary_en": "In one UK district hospital (Southend, 62 patients in a year, before-after) the yearly resection rate rose by 30% after video MDT meetings with a thoracic centre began; this is the relative rise that the 1.5-point assumption is built from.",
 "supported_en": "A 2004 abstract in the Journal of Telemedicine and Telecare reports a 30% relative rise in the yearly resection rate and a fall in the time from clinic to surgery from 69 to 54 days.",
 "not_supported_en": "The pages do not show the effect on the share of all lung cancer patients who get curative-intent treatment, and they include no controlled or Finnish data.",
 "in_use_here": "no_evidence",
 "in_use_scope": "none",
 "in_use_quote": null,
 "in_use_source": null,
 "in_use_summary_en": "No public sign was found that South Karelia's stage I–III lung cancer patients are routinely discussed by video with the HUS lung team; HUS says its own multidisciplinary group reviews patients only when needed.",
 "missing_en": "",
 "summary_en": "The HUS lung cancer pathway page says its multidisciplinary team reviews patients \"when needed\". No Ekhva or HUS page shows a video MDT with HUS for every stage I–III patient from South Karelia. The only effect evidence read is a 2004 UK before-after study of 62 patients, where the resection rate rose by 30% (relative). That supports the direction of the effect, but it is small, old and indirect for the assumed 1.5-point gain.",
 "unanswered_en": "Three searches found no Ekhva or HUS page that says how South Karelia's lung cancer treatment decisions are reviewed together with HUS, or whether any such meeting runs by video.",
