 "verdict_en": "No public sign that it is running in South Karelia. Evidence supports that it works, but not the size of effect we assume. Supported: A 2004 abstract in the Journal of Telemedicine and Telecare reports a 30% relative rise in the yearly resection rate and a fall in the time from clinic to surgery from 69 to 54 days. Not supported: The pages do not show the effect on the share of all lung cancer patients who get curative-intent treatment, and they include no controlled or Finnish data.",
